Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a4xx: Leave the VMIDMT out of the A430 crash dump

On MSM8994 the secure world owns the A430's VMIDMT (0x1000-0x1380). When
hangcheck recovered a GPU lockup, the crash-state capture read register
0x1000 and took a synchronous external abort in adreno_gpu_state_get(),
killing the GPU worker, so the GPU was never recovered:

  RBBM | AHB bus error | READ | addr=0x1000 | ports=0x0:0xB
  Internal error: synchronous external abort: 0000000096000010 [#1] SMP
  pc : adreno_gpu_state_get+0x204/0x254 [msm]
   a4xx_gpu_state_get+0x40/0x80 [msm]
   msm_gpu_crashstate_capture+0x60/0x568 [msm]
   recover_worker+0x274/0x43c [msm]

Give the A430 its own register list without the VMIDMT block.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.c	2026-10-18 18:13:26.687121643 -0600
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.c	2026-10-18 18:24:30.320962321 -0600
@@ -502,6 +502,87 @@
 	~0 /* sentinel */
 };
 
